  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Carbon monoxide does not react with water to form an acid.</p><p>The carbon monoxide molecule is one that won&#39;t react with water at all.&nbsp;As the acidic oxide has a higher oxidation state, it reacts with water to produce acid, and reacts with base to produce salt.&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mfenced><mi>steam</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>CO</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>CO</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>CO</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math>&nbsp;both reactions are carried out at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1270</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> temp. with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ni</mi></math> catalyst</p>",
